From 77acf3228ae91d1ab0cac70987a77cf0194284a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abdelhafid DJIDEL <266947999+hafid-logic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 10:20:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(core): pin write console-only fd set and netlink ACK
 kind gate

### What
Pins two admission gates in ginux-core: `write(1)` admits only stdout/stderr (fd 0 and 3 rejected), and `loopback_netlink_ack_index` retires a sequence only for NLMSG_ERROR (kind 2) messages, never for other kinds.

### Why it matters
Both are fail-closed contract gates. The existing suite pins write byte counts and netlink framing/alignment but not the fd set nor the message-kind gate, so widening either passes it.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| write fd set `1 \| 2` -> `0 \| 1 \| 2` | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| drop `kind == 2` netlink gate | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Spec-Ref: write(2) console-only surface; RFC 3549 / netlink(7) NLMSG_ERROR acknowledgement framing.

Baseline (clean tree + new test): PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-core --lib write_admission_rejects`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
index 65dbf923..374207ef 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-core/src/lib.rs
@@ -1025,4 +1025,23 @@ mod tests {
         assert!(balanced_arguments_allowed(SYS_WAIT4, u64::MAX, 0, 0));
         assert!(balanced_arguments_allowed(SYS_WAIT4, 1, 0, 0));
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn write_admission_rejects_stdin_and_netlink_requires_ack_kind() {
+        // write(1) is console-only: stdin (fd 0) must never be admitted
+        assert!(!balanced_arguments_allowed(1, 0, 0x1000, 1));
+        assert!(balanced_arguments_allowed(1, 1, 0x1000, 1));
+        assert!(balanced_arguments_allowed(1, 2, 0x1000, 1));
+        assert!(!balanced_arguments_allowed(1, 3, 0x1000, 1));
+        // a well-formed non-ACK message (kind=3) must not retire a sequence
+        let mut msg = [0u8; 20];
+        msg[0..4].copy_from_slice(&20u32.to_ne_bytes());
+        msg[4..6].copy_from_slice(&3u16.to_ne_bytes());
+        msg[8..12].copy_from_slice(&7u32.to_ne_bytes());
+        msg[16..20].copy_from_slice(&0i32.to_ne_bytes());
+        assert_eq!(loopback_netlink_ack_index(&msg, &[7]), Ok(None));
+        // same bytes with kind=2 do retire it
+        msg[4..6].copy_from_slice(&2u16.to_ne_bytes());
+        assert_eq!(loopback_netlink_ack_index(&msg, &[7]), Ok(Some(0)));
+    }
 }
